# Line endings (2026-09-06, compact UI slice 1 fix round 1).
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is the Git for Windows default, so a fresh clone on a
# Windows machine checks text files out with CRLF. Two things in this repo
# compare file BYTES and break when that happens:
#
#   web/src/tokens.css   — generated by web/scripts/tokens.mjs, which emits
#                          \n, and pinned byte-for-byte by src/tokens.test.ts.
#                          The drift gate is the only thing making "generated,
#                          never hand-edited" true, and it must hold on every
#                          machine, not only the one that wrote the file.
#   the i18n catalogs    — scripts/contrast.mjs and the parity checks read
#                          them as text; JSON is LF everywhere by convention
#                          and a CRLF checkout shows the whole file as changed
#                          the moment anything rewrites it.
#
# Everything else keeps Git's own detection.
* text=auto

web/src/tokens.css text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
web/src/index.css text eol=lf
